---
title: Homemade Chinese-Style Crispy Duck in a Pancake
servings: 12
prepTime: 15 min
cookTime: 1 hr
totalTime: 1h15m
Rating: 10/10
description: Use Mandarin Pancakes recipe from Essential Asian cookbook, half batch; or the recipe from TheSpruceEats.com is also good.
source: https://tasty.co/recipe/homemade-chinese-style-crispy-duck-in-a-pancake
tags: Duck
---

Preheat the oven to 325°F.

Lightly score into the skin of the @duck{2%pieces}(legs or breasts).

In boiling hot @water{4%cups}(boiling), add @soft brown sugar{6%tbsp} and @rice vinegar{2/3%cup}. Stir.

Submerge the duck pieces in the glaze mix for ~{20%seconds} each.
Pad dry the duck legs with paper towel.

In a #small bowl{}, mix the @onion powder{1%tbsp}, @ginger{1/4%cup}(fresh grated, or 2 tsp ground ginger),
@salt{4%tbsp}, @Chinese five spice{2%tbsp}, and @soft brown sugar{2%tbsp}.
Coat the duck thoroughly in the seasoning mix.

Place the duck on a #cooling rack{} set over a #baking tray{}, skin side up.
Roast the duck for ~{30%minutes}.

Turn up the oven to 400˚F and roast the duck for another ~{20%minutes}.

Rest the duck legs for ~{20%minutes}, then shred them with two forks or slice into thin strips.

Serve with @./Breads/Mandarin_Pancakes{12}, @hoisin sauce{1/4%cup}, @spring onions{4}(sliced on bias), and @cucumber{1}(seedless, sliced).

= Nutritional Information (per serving) =
Calories 285 | Fat 6g | Carbs 41g | Fiber 1g | Sugar 16g | Protein 14g
